{
  "title": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling \u2014 attribution",
  "description": "Two metrics, read side by side during a k6 run: request latency, and DynamoDB throttle events (ReadThrottleEvents / WriteThrottleEvents). Nothing on this dashboard computes a verdict about which resource was the ceiling \u2014 the four-row attribution table that used to do that was deleted on 2026-09-01. Every other panel is context for those two.",
  "tags": [
    "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "table_name",
        "type": "textbox",
        "label": "DynamoDB table",
        "description": "Table name used in every DynamoDB CloudWatch dimension on this dashboard.",
        "query": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
        "current": {
          "text": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
          "value": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1. Latency and DynamoDB throttling",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "DynamoDB throttle events (read and write)",
      "description": "Was DynamoDB rejecting us? Non-zero means yes — DynamoDB refused requests, and the SDK retried them with backoff inside the service. Both series are plotted: ReadThrottleEvents and WriteThrottleEvents are two separate lines, not a total. Read this beside the latency panels; nothing here decides for you — the four-row attribution table that used to do that was deleted on 2026-09-01 after it named the service while DynamoDB was rejecting 5588 reads/minute. Reads throttle first on this table: at the 55/15/25/5 mix the capacity model costs 1.025 RCU per request against 0.2 WCU, so reads bind near 24 rps and writes not until ~125 rps. Measured 2026-09-01 at 250 rps: ReadThrottleEvents peaked at 5588/min while WriteThrottleEvents stayed at zero. WriteThrottleEvents rising while the read line stays flat is about write capacity specifically, not the table as a whole. Both are per-minute counts at table level. ThrottledRequests is deliberately not shown: it reads zero at instants during sustained throttling.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ReadThrottleEvents",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "WriteThrottleEvents",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "2. DynamoDB server-side latency (the uncontaminated clock)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "SuccessfulRequestLatency by operation (Average & Maximum)",
      "description": "The DynamoDB-reported clock, split by GetItem/PutItem/Query. This is what db_wall_avg_by_route is compared against \u2014 that metric is wall-clock around the SDK await and absorbs event-loop queueing (measured 12.1x inflation with the database unchanged), so a gap between this panel and it is the queueing signal, not extra DB time. Read that gap PER ROUTE: each route is compared against the sum of only the operations it issues (/reports issues Query then PutItem), which is what the \"Queueing delay by route\" panel computes. db_ms was the k6 Trend that carried this number before the SLI moved into the service; it no longer exists. Average and Maximum both shown: Maximum surfaces tail spikes Average hides.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "SuccessfulRequestLatency",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name",
            "Operation": [
              "GetItem",
              "PutItem",
              "Query"
            ]
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "SuccessfulRequestLatency",
          "statistic": "Maximum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name",
            "Operation": [
              "GetItem",
              "PutItem",
              "Query"
            ]
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "3. Capacity headroom (saturation as convergence, not a number)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Read capacity: consumed vs provisioned",
      "description": "Consumed*CapacityUnits is a Sum-per-period metric (units used in the preceding 60s); Provisioned*CapacityUnits is already expressed as units/second. To compare them as rates, divide the consumed line by 60 (the period below) \u2014 this panel shows the raw values, not pre-divided. Consumed converging on or crossing provisioned is read capacity becoming the ceiling, and should line up with ReadThrottleEvents in row 1.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ConsumedReadCapacityUnits",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ProvisionedReadCapacityUnits",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Write capacity: consumed vs provisioned",
      "description": "Same units caveat as the read panel: ConsumedWriteCapacityUnits is Sum-per-60s, ProvisionedWriteCapacityUnits is already units/second \u2014 divide consumed by 60 to compare rates. Convergence here should line up with WriteThrottleEvents in row 1.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ConsumedWriteCapacityUnits",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ProvisionedWriteCapacityUnits",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "4. Service (ECS) \u2014 what the task itself was doing",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "ECS CPUUtilization (Average & Maximum)",
      "description": "CPU against the 0.25 vCPU task allocation. Read it beside the throttle-events panel, not in isolation: during the 2026-09-01 throttling incident CPU sat at 3\u201316% while event-loop utilization read 1.000, because SDK retry backoff on a throttled DynamoDB call saturates the event loop without burning CPU. Low CPU here is not evidence the service was idle.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "CPUUtilization",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
            "ServiceName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "CPUUtilization",
          "statistic": "Maximum",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
            "ServiceName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "ECS MemoryUtilization (Average & Maximum)",
      "description": "Memory pressure is a confound worth ruling out: if memory is climbing toward the task limit, latency may be about the container rather than about anything else shown here.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 29
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "MemoryUtilization",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
            "ServiceName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "${cloudwatch_datasource_uid}"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/ECS",
          "metricName": "MemoryUtilization",
          "statistic": "Maximum",
          "dimensions": {
            "ClusterName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
            "ServiceName": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
